<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/">
	<!-- A row Core draws itself on its Settings pages: a paragraph, a note or a status list line (SET-R5, SET-R10,
	SET-R11). Its frames come from their own pool in the panel's list, and Blizzard's list draws one through the stock
	InitFrame and Resetter, which call the frame's Init and Release (adapter/Settings.lua, PagleSettingsRowMixin), so
	Core writes no field onto an initializer (SET-R6). Its height is the row's height: 26, as Blizzard's controls. -->
	<Frame name="PagleSettingsRowTemplate" mixin="PagleSettingsRowMixin" virtual="true">
		<Size x="280" y="26"/>
	</Frame>
	<!-- A slot dropdown's row (SET-R51, adapter/LookAndFeel.lua, PagleSettingsSlotRowMixin): the slot's label and its
	dropdown on a native row's 26 pixels, and "{N} more in the Curio Shop" under the dropdown, so 46 in all. Its own
	pool, drawn through the stock InitFrame and Resetter as Core's other rows (SET-R6). -->
	<Frame name="PagleSettingsSlotRowTemplate" mixin="PagleSettingsSlotRowMixin" virtual="true">
		<Size x="280" y="46"/>
	</Frame>
	<!-- A Module's keybinding row (SET-R20, adapter/KeyBindingRow.lua, PagleSettingsKeyRowMixin): its label and its two
	keys, greyed out by its isEnabled, which Blizzard's KeyBindingFrameBindingTemplate never reads (#120). Its own pool,
	drawn through the stock InitFrame and Resetter as Core's other rows (SET-R6). 26 pixels, as Core's text rows. -->
	<Frame name="PagleSettingsKeyRowTemplate" mixin="PagleSettingsKeyRowMixin" virtual="true">
		<Size x="280" y="26"/>
	</Frame>
	<!-- The news sign (core/news-sign.md): its art's atlases, its frame and drawing kit, its six looks, and its dev
	command. Loaded here because the TOC's file lines are hashed by pagle-backend's ranked policy (PRJ-R64), so a new
	file there would need a new rule set; an XML file's <Script> lines aren't. Nothing in them runs before login but
	the tables they define. -->
	<Script file="..\data\NewsSignArt.lua"/>
	<Script file="NewsSign.lua"/>
	<Script file="NewsSignLooks.lua"/>
	<Script file="NewsSignDev.lua"/>
	<!-- Party toasts and cheers (announcements.md ANN-R103–R109, ANN-R112, settings.md SET-R36; from 1.5.2, #640) load here, after
	adapter/Settings.lua: a patch can't add a file to the TOC, whose file list is hashed, and every file in logic/ is
	hashed too. Their messages' pure Lua first, then the client's side, the party toast's frame and the Party block.
	Each looks up what it needs of files loaded later (the lanes, PagleDB) when it runs. Paths are relative to this
	file. -->
	<Script file="PartyMessages.lua"/>
	<Script file="Party.lua"/>
	<Script file="PartyToast.lua"/>
	<Script file="PartySettings.lua"/>
	<!-- The Morning Tide's section on the Announcements page (settings.md SET-R37, from 1.6), after the Party block's,
	which adapter/AnnouncementSettings.lua calls before it. -->
	<Script file="NewsSignSettings.lua"/>
</Ui>
